From 86ba704856b035f13ff3f486553b611337ee0993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Olvin <>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:07:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: UAC voice transport (ALSA) for Quectel EC25

- new 'alsadev' device setting enables UAC mode (ALSA capture/playback
  instead of the serial audio tty); data tty stays required
- alsa_card_init()/soundcard_init(): open 8 kHz s16 mono capture and
  playback streams, the capture poll fd feeds the channel select loop
- channel read/write: accumulate ALSA partial reads into 20 ms frames;
  write frames directly to the playback stream with EPIPE recovery
- activate/disactivate call: start/drop the ALSA streams per call
- dial/answer: arm AT+QPCMV=1,2 (USB audio) before ATD/ATA and skip the
  post-dial AT+QPCMV=1,0 in UAC mode
- monitor: skip the tty status check for the ALSA capture fd
- link against libasound

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
